# Strips are output. `input/` is the source: a design run reads it and writes
# strips/<device>/, replacing whatever was there. Nothing under strips/ is
# tracked — re-run to regenerate.
#
# Worth knowing: a run is not deterministic. The agent makes the design
# decisions, and none of them live in input/, so re-running the same input
# produces a *different* strip rather than the same one back. Copy a strip
# folder somewhere outside the repo if you want to keep a particular result.
strips/**

strip_editor/node_modules/
strip_editor/package-lock.json

# Vite's production bundle. This project runs as a dev server; `npm run build`
# exists to prove the app still compiles, and its output is not shipped.
strip_editor/dist/

# Reference galleries — the category folders under composer/references/, not the
# two documents beside them (README.md and history.md), which are
# ours and stay tracked.
#
# These are screenshots of store pages by other people, kept as local anchors
# for the design skill's review step. They are someone else's copyrighted work:
# fine to hold on your own disk as reference, not ours to redistribute under
# this repo's MIT licence. composer/references/README.md has always said so.
composer/references/*/
composer/references/history.md

# macOS Finder droppings.
.DS_Store

input/
!input/README.md

# Personal Claude Code overrides. The committed .claude/settings.json is the
# shared one; this file is yours and is not shipped.
.claude/settings.local.json

# design-ss run state: pid/pgid of the current run, the agent log, the last
# render JSON. Local to a checkout, never shared.
.design-ss/
